WEBVTT

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:03.340
My passionate Idol Activities,

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:06.350
Aikatsu! is about to start!

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:14.240
Sakura-chan, what're you doing?

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.960
This is a statue of Masquerade, is it not?

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:21.040
That's right. They're the legendary idols Hime and Miya.

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:24.290
This one is Miya-san, and that is Hime-san.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.850
She's the current Headmistress, Mitsuishi Orihime.

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:28.590
You sure know your stuff.

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:30.920
Their debut was twenty years ago.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:34.220
They became top idols in the blink of an eye,

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:38.670
and were considered the twin stars of the idol world throughout their career.

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:44.690
Even today, they hold the records for both show attendance and record sales.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:45.950
How amazing.

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:49.120
But when they were at the peak of their popularity, they suddenly disbanded.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:51.710
Their legendary farewell concert at the Budokan

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:55.320
made over a million fans nationwide cry their hearts out.

00:00:55.960 --> 00:01:00.290
Since then, Miya hasn't made a single public appearance.

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:02.550
Why did they disband?

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:04.280
There are quite a few theories.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:08.540
Some say they disagreed about what direction to take their music.

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:11.430
Others think that Miya was injured and unable to continue dancing.

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:14.550
Either way, the truth remains unknown.

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:18.050
It's considered the biggest mystery in the idol world.

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:19.520
You know everything, Aoi!

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:22.180
I've got all of Masquerade's info stored up here.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:25.170
One day, I'll become a top idol as well.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.500
Mother's Day is almost here!

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:09.560
I wonder why it's on the second Sunday of May?

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:13.780
We inherited the tradition of Mother's Day from America.

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:18.420
The second Sunday of May is the anniversary of a big women's rights movement.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:23.040
Yurika-chan, what sort of person is your mother?

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:27.170
Like me, she's a vampire. The great and noble Carmilla-sama. {it's the name of a vampire book}{I swear I looked it up properly before...}

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:28.800
Carmilla-sama?

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:30.550
What about yours, Sakura-chan?

00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:32.060
My mother?

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:34.940
It's the Kitaouji Theater!

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:38.160
Possessing a heart as noble as a blade,

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:43.530
she stands atop all theater...

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:43.530
Stop!

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.290
Sakura, will this take a while?

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:48.540
I suppose so. It should take me about an hour and a half.

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:51.330
Seems like we'd be here until long after break ends.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:52.660
We probably shouldn't skip class for it.

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:56.600
Oh no! I still haven't eaten my strawberry rice cake pudding!

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:02.840
My strawberry rice cake pudding!

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:08.350
Everyhoney, we've decided on your next audition.

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:10.350
It's the Nostamelo Girl live audition!

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:16.740
Nostamelo is short for "nostalgic melody".

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:19.860
To put it simply, a song that'll make your mother and father think,

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:23.360
"Ah, how nostalgic!" Understand?

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:27.370
The song for the audition is the famous piece, "Wake up my music"!

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:30.450
"Wake up my music" is a Masquerade song!

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:31.630
Yes!

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:34.000
It's our Academy Mother's song!

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:35.710
Give it everything you've got. {split}

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:39.000
The lady herself will be watching it, after all.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:42.910
And because it's a Masquerade song, the audition will be held in pairs.

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:45.970
In other words, you'll be a duo. A combo. Buddies.

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:49.260
You will take on this audition in groups of two.

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:51.070
Give it your all, honeys!

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:52.270
Okay!

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:55.830
What kind of song is "Wake up my music"?

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:56.440
What?

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:57.760
You've never heard it?

00:04:57.760 --> 00:04:58.650
I haven't.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:04:59.520
Me neither.

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:00.570
I haven't either.

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:01.780
Nor Yurika-sama.

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:03.150
How can this be...

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:08.990
"Wake up my music" is a famous song that cemented Masquerade's status as a top idol group.

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:10.670
These are pictures from their performance.

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:12.790
They look even more mysterious than their statue.

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:16.380
I can certainly see why they are said to have influenced an entire generation.

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:18.860
It's a Love You that surpasses time!

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:23.420
I bet tasting the blood of such legendary idols is to die for.

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:24.800
Anyway!

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:27.430
Let's get to special training for the Nostamelo Girl audition!

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:29.180
Yeah!

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:32.180
Time really does fly by, doesn't it?

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:33.680
Miya...

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:39.690
Ai...katsu!

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:42.690
What's up with this training?

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:46.200
Nostalgic training is just the thing we need!

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:48.290
I'm sure of it!

00:05:48.290 --> 00:05:50.200
This is way too heavy!

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:53.360
S-So this is "retro training"...

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:54.700
Hey, Yurika!

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:56.890
Why are you skipping out on training?

00:05:56.890 --> 00:06:00.460
I'll become a pile of ash if I bask in that much sunlight.

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:04.680
Aikatsu!

00:06:07.550 --> 00:06:10.090
Is this nostalgic training too?

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:13.350
That's right.

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:16.350
They're called "supermodel training braces". {da to omou}

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:22.710
They're so tight...

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:26.240
Don't give up, Otome! Yurika's still with us!

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:32.990
With Yurika-sama's vampiric power and the strength of tomato juice, this is no problem at all.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:37.000
Otome's Love You power also...

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:41.240
Ai-katsu... Ai-katsu...

00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:43.670
I'm beat...

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:47.090
I wonder how this will improve my kabuki acting...

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:48.390
I know!

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:49.720
Go ahead, Kiriya-kun.

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:53.200
"Wake up my music" is Masquerade's song.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:56.430
In other words, a pair. A duo. A combo!

00:06:56.610 --> 00:06:58.280
In other words, what?

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:02.100
I think we should practice for this in pairs.

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:04.230
Should we pick our own partners?

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:06.230
We should be fair and pick randomly.

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:11.020
There are a lot of ways to do it, but I think the fairest way is to use rock-paper-scissors.

00:07:11.020 --> 00:07:12.290
No complaints here.

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:13.620
Sounds good!

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:17.580
Rock-paper-scissors to split us into groups!

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:38.140
You sure love the shade.

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:40.410
You'll just fail again if you don't train.

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:42.380
I-If it's only about three seconds...

00:07:42.380 --> 00:07:44.770
If you can do it for three, then do it for ten!

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:46.850
If you can do it for ten seconds, then run for two hours!

00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:48.440
T-Two hours?!

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:50.700
I'll turn into ash...

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:52.700
Hold it!

00:07:53.810 --> 00:07:56.080
Our training's definitely gonna pay off.

00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:59.190
Aikatsu! Aikatsu!

00:07:59.190 --> 00:08:01.710
Aikatsu! Aikatsu!

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:10.210
<i>Raise the volume and wake up love!</i>

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:13.200
If I knew you were this bad,

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:17.720
I would have just stayed home and made some extra cash making artificial flowers instead. {I think it's the flowers}

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:20.260
Looks like the training <i>didn't</i> pay off.

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:23.080
I can't feel even the tiniest bit of that training.

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:26.620
Effort without results is meaningless.

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:31.490
Imagine that there's a gap two meters wide here.

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:33.680
Even if a girl who could only jump one meter

00:08:33.690 --> 00:08:37.990
trained her hardest to jump one meter and ninety-nine centimeters,

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:39.980
would she not still fall?

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:48.160
"And now I'm back in my room."

00:08:51.210 --> 00:08:53.430
You're tweeting on KiraKiratter? {changed to caps the K} {that's fine, I guess}

00:08:53.430 --> 00:08:55.560
Ah, I almost forgot!

00:08:58.180 --> 00:08:59.570
Wh-What?

00:08:59.570 --> 00:09:01.830
I've gotta take some pics for Mother's Day.

00:09:07.030 --> 00:09:10.190
But why pictures of <i>me</i> for Mother's Day? I don't get it.

00:09:14.270 --> 00:09:17.070
Look at all these pics of Aoi-neesan!

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:18.800
Thanks a bunch, Onee-chan!

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:21.990
I couldn't help it knowing how much you like Aoi.

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:24.580
But Raichi, we need to hurry up.

00:09:24.980 --> 00:09:26.580
Oh yeah!

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:29.060
Mom!

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:32.090
Thanks for always taking care of us!

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:36.890
Thanks so much, you two!

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:42.630
Why are you cutting the stems underwater?

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:45.410
If you do it like this they'll take up water right away.

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:49.020
They're gorgeous.

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:50.780
This means a lot to me.

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:54.170
Oh, if you're dressed like that...

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:59.030
Today's Mother's Day, so Onee-chan and I decided to help you out even more than usual.

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:02.030
You don't have to do a single thing today, Mama.

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:04.120
It's even Sunday, so just relax.

00:10:25.240 --> 00:10:28.070
Raichi, let's get to spring cleaning!

00:10:28.070 --> 00:10:29.180
Roger!

00:10:46.030 --> 00:10:47.960
Even though we're used to helping out...

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:50.960
Spring cleaning really takes a lot out of you.

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:55.460
Mom sure is amazing.

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:59.300
We're not done yet! This isn't even my final idol form! {sure}

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:00.280
Right!

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:09.310
Mama, we're about done here.

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:11.500
Huh, where's Mom?

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:13.970
I guess there's still preparation to do even during a holiday.

00:11:16.670 --> 00:11:18.610
Mama, what're you cooking?

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:20.360
Kinpira veggies.

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:22.990
Your kinpira veggie recipe is awesome.

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:25.170
The customers all love it.

00:11:25.170 --> 00:11:29.120
It's just a simple home-cooked meal.

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:31.620
Hey Mama, how do you make it?

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:35.920
First you cut the vegetables into thin strips, and then stir-fry it a little in sesame oil.

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:37.440
Oh, I see.

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:41.270
Then put in sake, mirin, and soy sauce to taste,

00:11:41.270 --> 00:11:43.800
and it's done when it boils off.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:45.140
It's a simple recipe.

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:48.320
How much sake and mirin and stuff do you use?

00:11:48.320 --> 00:11:49.640
Let's see...

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:51.640
Just enough?

00:11:52.510 --> 00:11:54.160
What does "just enough" mean?

00:11:55.450 --> 00:12:00.450
I'm always making a lot of it, so I can't spare the time to perfectly measure it out every time.

00:12:00.450 --> 00:12:03.680
If you make it a lot, your body will learn to measure it by eye.

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:05.660
Wow, that sounds hard. {eh... sure}

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:08.160
And there we go!

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:09.320
Want to taste it for me?

00:12:09.320 --> 00:12:10.090
Sure!

00:12:13.050 --> 00:12:13.920
Careful, it's hot.

00:12:18.970 --> 00:12:20.340
Delicious!

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:22.030
Home cooking's the best!

00:12:22.030 --> 00:12:24.930
It's amazing how it turns out the same even though you do it by eye!

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:27.480
You think so? Isn't Aikatsu the same?

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:28.240
Huh?

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:32.410
If you try learning the dance by memorizing how your right hand goes or left leg steps,

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:34.440
it's really hard to get it right.

00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:38.400
All you can do is practice and practice until your body remembers on its own.

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:41.190
You've hit a wall, haven't you?

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:43.190
How can you tell?

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:50.550
Other people may not be able to tell, but I'm your mother.

00:12:50.550 --> 00:12:52.200
I can see right through you.

00:12:53.650 --> 00:12:58.110
My next gig is called the Nostamelo Girl live audition.

00:12:58.110 --> 00:13:00.210
I just can't get the piece down right.

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:03.370
I'm giving it my all with Aoi in practice, but still...

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:04.720
What kind of song is it?

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:06.720
It's "Wake up my music".

00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:09.970
Now that <i>is</i> a nostalgic song.

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:12.730
Did you used to sing it at karaoke and stuff?

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:15.730
Of course I did! It was one of my favorites.

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:18.230
How about we go for a little walk together?

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:33.590
We used to come to this park all the time.

00:13:33.590 --> 00:13:34.910
I still remember.

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:37.580
I played with Dad a lot here.

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:39.420
Look! Remember that tree?

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:43.870
You and Dad had a contest to see who could climb higher up this tree.

00:13:43.870 --> 00:13:48.090
He broke a branch and fell off, and then the park supervisor got mad at him.

00:13:50.820 --> 00:13:53.700
I brought you here to show you this.

00:13:53.700 --> 00:13:55.490
It really brings back memories.

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:02.230
I sang up here a lot when I was younger.

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:06.450
That's right. I can still remember you singing for us like it was yesterday.

00:14:07.470 --> 00:14:11.450
Here was the first step on your path to becoming an idol.

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:13.290
It really might've been.

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:16.480
But you know, you're not the only one who started out here.

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:17.440
Huh?

00:14:17.440 --> 00:14:19.210
This stage is old.

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:22.460
It's been here since before I was even born.

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:26.500
Do you mean that you used to sing here too?

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:27.970
Just a bit.

00:14:28.850 --> 00:14:32.470
As a little girl, I loved singing up on this stage.

00:14:33.590 --> 00:14:36.470
I wasn't singing to anyone but myself.

00:14:36.470 --> 00:14:40.600
Up on stage, the spotlight was all mine.

00:14:42.360 --> 00:14:45.440
The applause was all for me.

00:14:46.710 --> 00:14:49.360
Of course, it was all just pretend.

00:14:49.710 --> 00:14:51.940
But acting like an idol was a lot of fun.

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:58.140
As I grew older, whenever things got tough and I was feeling down,

00:14:58.140 --> 00:15:00.480
I came here to sing alone.

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:06.290
This is also where I met your father.

00:15:07.610 --> 00:15:09.890
It was a cold winter day.

00:15:09.890 --> 00:15:15.020
It was snowing, but I felt like I needed to sing no matter what.

00:15:16.530 --> 00:15:20.890
As I finished and was just starting to feel a bit better,

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:24.360
I heard the sound of applause.

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:26.400
The sound of one person clapping.

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:34.830
There was all this snow piled up on your father's shoulders,

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:40.410
and I realized that he had been standing in the snow listening to me this whole time.

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:43.540
That's a wonderful story.

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:47.640
Even though it's May already, it's still quite cold sitting here on the stone.

00:15:49.010 --> 00:15:51.430
How about we hold a concert here together?

00:15:53.060 --> 00:15:54.000
Sure!

00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:57.270
It's our first performance!

00:15:57.930 --> 00:15:59.430
How exciting!

00:16:00.900 --> 00:16:02.440
And now that we've got these... {holy shit, it's literally oshamoji -> maiku}

00:16:02.750 --> 00:16:04.220
Let's do it!

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:16.450
<i>I wonder if you've realized that I change a bit every day</i>

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:25.460
<i>I'm at my most beautiful singing by your side</i>

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:48.830
<i>The sunlight gathers in my chiffon blouse</i>

00:16:48.830 --> 00:16:55.980
<i>The beating of my heart signals the way</i>

00:16:57.640 --> 00:16:59.710
Well? Do you get it now?

00:16:59.710 --> 00:17:00.990
I think so!

00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:06.120
I just need to practice until my body remembers, just like how you make kinpira.

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:08.950
And then even <i>I'll</i> be able to jump two meters!

00:17:08.950 --> 00:17:09.870
What?

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:12.010
Don't worry about it.

00:17:13.030 --> 00:17:14.350
Oh, one more thing.

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:16.700
I have something for you.

00:17:18.190 --> 00:17:19.610
An Aikatsu card!

00:17:19.610 --> 00:17:22.370
But why do you have this?!

00:17:24.950 --> 00:17:28.770
Every girl dreams of becoming an idol.

00:17:37.470 --> 00:17:38.820
Thanks!

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:40.320
I'll use it well. {eh, it's okay}

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:42.660
Okay.

00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:44.100
I know you will.

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:47.720
Hey, are you going to come to my next audition?

00:17:47.720 --> 00:17:49.050
I wouldn't miss it!

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:54.670
Aikatsu! Aikatsu!

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:56.740
Ichigo looks really pumped up.

00:17:56.740 --> 00:18:00.180
I guess she charged up when she went home.

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:02.180
Aikatsu! Aikatsu!

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:11.570
Everyhoney, are you ready?

00:18:11.570 --> 00:18:14.230
And, we have a special guest today!

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:18.570
Angely Sugar's top designer, Amahane Asuka-san is visiting us today!

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:20.750
Welcome, Asuka-san!

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:24.620
Nostamelo Girl live audition...

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:25.830
Let's start!

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:29.580
We're up next.

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:30.330
Right.

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:33.340
<i>Mama, watch me.</i>

00:19:45.730 --> 00:19:48.030
That's the Starlight Tiara!

00:21:39.270 --> 00:21:43.870
It's been over ten years since we last saw the Starlight Tiara. {juusuu, not suujuu}

00:21:43.870 --> 00:21:44.740
You're right.

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:48.780
It makes you feel like a new legend is being born. {arata, not anata}

00:21:48.780 --> 00:21:52.790
Victory goes to the Hoshimiya-Kiriya pair!

00:21:53.710 --> 00:21:54.840
Mama!

00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:56.620
Ichigo!

00:21:57.420 --> 00:22:00.390
Thank you! I was able to win because of you!

00:22:00.390 --> 00:22:02.820
I glad you could make use of that card.

00:22:04.010 --> 00:22:06.630
But it all boils down to your own efforts. {like kinpira, get it?} {but you fry kinpira}{boil the saucy parts}

00:22:07.130 --> 00:22:10.440
It was thanks to you that I was able to come this far.

00:22:12.370 --> 00:22:15.140
I'm glad you grew up to be such a wonderful girl.

00:23:55.630 --> 00:23:57.740
This week's Aikatsu Aphorism!

00:23:59.040 --> 00:24:01.780
Do you have a favorite food from back home too?

00:24:01.780 --> 00:24:03.140
Probably Mom's beef stew.

00:24:03.140 --> 00:24:04.720
It's spicy and delicious!

00:24:04.720 --> 00:24:06.770
I can't help but get the urge to eat it sometimes!

00:24:07.420 --> 00:24:09.880
Nothing beats home cooking.

00:24:10.440 --> 00:24:13.850
Listen to this! I got the chance to appear in an Angely Sugar commercial!

00:24:13.850 --> 00:24:15.800
Doesn't that conflict with our next concert?

00:24:15.800 --> 00:24:16.760
It's gonna be tough.

00:24:16.760 --> 00:24:19.060
Don't worry! I'll give both of them 100%!

00:24:19.060 --> 00:24:20.560
Next time on Aikatsu!

00:24:20.560 --> 00:24:21.470
Ichigo Panic.

00:24:21.470 --> 00:24:23.840
Always passionate, Idol Activities!
